<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9309" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνοσμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνοδμος</span>
			, <i>without smell,</i>
			v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Acut.</u>
				63
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				634b19
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴχνη ἄνοσμα</span>
			footsteps <i>that leave no scent,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				5.12
			</span></i>:—but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄοσμος</span>
			(q.v.) was preferred.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
